  "parent": "pt-BR",
  "notes": "Pernambucano (Recife). Northeastern type. Two strongest north/south isoglosses: (1) NO /t,d/ palatalisation — tia -> [ˈtiɐ], leite -> [ˈlejtɪ] (ALiB: ~10% palatalisation in Recife); (2) open pretonic vowels /e/ -> [ɛ], /o/ -> [ɔ] (menino -> [mɛˈninʊ], boneca -> [bɔˈnɛkɐ]). Coda /S/ palatalised to [ʃ,ʒ] (Recife chiado). Strong dorsal onset /r/; coda /R/ -> aspiration.",
  "quality": "research",
